{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011Cf7SQhHNcNSogJYdPaANZ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect. Now I have a comprehensive understanding of the codebase. Let me move to the design phase.\n\n```\n<<PHASE:DESIGN>>\n```\n\n**Proposed change, file by file:**\n\n1. **ApiError.kt** — Add a new error code `SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATUS` to the `ErrorCode` enum. This will be used when attempting to confirm a shipment that is in the `CANCELLED` state (or potentially any invalid state for confirmation).\n\n2. **ShipmentController.kt** — Add a new endpoint `POST /shipments/{shipmentId}/confirm` that:\n   - Retrieves the shipment by ID\n   - If not found, throws `ResourceNotFoundException` with `SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND`\n   - If found and status is `CREATED`, updates status to `CONFIRMED`, saves, and returns the updated shipment with HTTP 200\n   - If found and status is already `CONFIRMED`, returns the shipment as-is with HTTP 200 (idempotent)\n   - If found and status is `CANCELLED`, throws `ConflictException` with `SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATUS` and HTTP 409\n\n3. **ShipmentControllerTest.kt** — Add four new test cases:\n   - Test confirming a CREATED shipment transitions to CONFIRMED\n   - Test confirming an already CONFIRMED shipment returns the same shipment (idempotency)\n   - Test confirming a CANCELLED shipment returns 409 with appropriate error code\n   - Test confirming a non-existent shipment returns 404 with appropriate error code\n\n**Alternative considered and rejected:**\n- Add new service layer: Not necessary as the logic is simple and existing controllers operate directly with the repository. Existing patterns show this is acceptable for this codebase.\n- Use separate request/response DTOs: The existing API returns the entity directly (Shipment) without wrapper objects, so following that pattern is correct.\n- Add a general \"SHIPMENT_OPERATION_NOT_ALLOWED\" error code: More specific error codes are better for clients to handle different cases differently; `SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATUS` is more semantic.\n\n**Data and error flow:**\n\n| Case | Input | Read | Write | Output | HTTP |\n|------|-------|------|-------|--------|------|\n| Normal confirm | POST /shipments/S-1/confirm | Shipment S-1, status=CREATED | Update to status=CONFIRMED | Updated Shipment | 200 |\n| Idempotent confirm | POST /shipments/S-1/confirm | Shipment S-1, status=CONFIRMED | None (no change) | Shipment unchanged | 200 |\n| Cancelled reject | POST /shipments/S-1/confirm | Shipment S-1, status=CANCELLED | None | ErrorCode.SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATUS | 409 |\n| Not found | POST /shipments/missing/confirm | Nothing | None | ErrorCode.SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND | 404 |\n\n**Test strategy:**\n\n1. **Test 1: Confirm created shipment** — Creates a shipment in CREATED status, confirms it, verifies status changes to CONFIRMED and response contains the updated shipment.\n2. **Test 2: Confirm already confirmed shipment** — Creates a shipment, confirms it once, confirms it again, verifies the second confirm succeeds with same result (idempotency).\n3. **Test 3: Confirm cancelled shipment** — Directly inserts a CANCELLED shipment into the repository, attempts to confirm, verifies 409 response with SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATUS error code.\n4. **Test 4: Confirm non-existent shipment** — Attempts to confirm a shipment that does not exist, verifies 404 response with SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND error code.\n\n---\n\n```\n<<PHASE:IMPLEMENTATION>>\n```\n\nNow I'll implement the changes:"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":878,"cache_read_input_tokens":16660,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":878},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"82897f1e-2754-4320-a20b-48eafe820edf"